<title>USA: Advanced Machine to sell Pulsarr unit.</title>
<headline>Advanced Machine to sell Pulsarr unit.</headline>
<dateline>MEDFORD, Ore. 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Advanced Machine Vision Corp said on Tuesday it sold its Holland-based Pulsarr Holding BV unit to Barco NV of Belgium for $8.4 million in cash.</p>
<p>Advanced Machine said the sale would reduce 1997 sales volume by $6 million but would have a minimal impact on operating earnings.</p>
<p>The company said the sale would result in a $5 million gain, which primarily represents a recovery of the $4.9 million in Pulsarr in-process technology expensed in the first quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>Advanced Machine makes computer-aided vision defect detection systems.  Its shares were up 3/16 to 1-13/16 in mid-morning Nasdaq trading.</p>
